// Taking a place in the formation (the player: a rider whose place is in front should get there quickly, at its own
// speed, not eased in at little more than the citizens' pace): Continental (seed 101, start_epoch 12), 24 citizens
// (0.5 tiles/s) at 36,44 and 12 dragoons (0.8) six tiles behind them at 30,44, sent together 40 tiles east to 76,46 in
// one right-click - the formation puts the dragoons in the front rank, so they have to overtake the whole formation.
// `fmove watch 1` logs every unit every step (# fmwatch): a reader takes the time until the dragoons' middle is ahead
// of the citizens' middle along the move, and how far behind their final places they still are; fmove sum the rest.
// Found 2026-11-02 (game_seed 1): the dragoons are in front of the citizens at 15 s and march in their place from
// then on - the closing rule (groupmove.c ff_speed: the formation's speed plus FF_GAIN for each tile behind, capped
// at the unit's own top speed x formation_catchup) gives a 0.8 rider its full speed whenever it is more than 0.6
// tiles behind its place; a ramp straight to the cap changed nothing here. A rider seen held to the citizens' pace
// while taking its place is something else: the formation's own start, a re-form on the march, or a block.
wait_until(0.1min)
spawn(1, unit.citizen, 36, 44, 24)
spawn(1, unit.cav09_dragoon_gun, 30, 44, 12)
wait_until(0.4min)
cmd("fmove watch 1")
cmd("fmove go 1 33 44 10 76 46")
every(2s, 0.4min, 2.4min, (run) => {
    cmd("fmove stat")
})
wait_until(2.45min)
cmd("fmove sum")
cmd("fmove watch 0")
